From 98bee9ce39cd579fa666334f03e793b5faedd77b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:31:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0907 redfin: DRV2624 vibration motor on GENI SE9 I2C
 (sweethaptic=1)

TI DRV2624 (LRA, open loop, lito-redfin-haptics.dtsi values) at 0x5a on
QUPv3 wrapper 1 SE3 (0x98c000), I2C FIFO code from sweet_touch.c. Its
enable line PM7250B GPIO1 goes high through the APPS SPMI channel (as
shim/spmi.c), SE9 clocks from gcc-lito (XO), pins gpio46/47 function 1.
Brought up 8 s after start on its own thread; sweethaptic=2 also buzzes
once when ready. sweet_haptic_buzz(ms, strength) is the API; the poke /
USB command line "v MS [STRENGTH]" calls it (tools/flame-cmd.py 'v 200').
Not yet hooked to iOS (iPhone X haptics go through its audio path).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GizUhEzkc6MoTcLnCZCfFa
